# Line-ending policy
#
# The repository stores every text file with LF. Windows editors that rewrite a
# file with CRLF used to show up as a whole-file diff (a 37-line Makefile edit
# appeared as 608 changed lines), which buried real changes during review.
# `text=auto` lets git detect text vs binary; `eol=lf` pins the stored form.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch scripts are launched by cmd.exe and keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never diffed, never normalized.
*.png   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.TTF   binary
*.a     binary
*.piskel binary
*.dat   binary

# Vendored third-party code keeps its upstream formatting; the pre-commit
# whitespace check does not apply to it.
Game/include/cglm/** -whitespace
